<overview>
<p>Motorized infantry platoons use light ground vehicles, typically motorcycles or quad bikes, for rapid movement between positions. Faster than foot infantry and cheaper than fully mechanized formations, motorized platoons fill the gap between static garrison troops and armored combat units. They excel at road-bound patrol routes, rapid redeployment along prepared axes, and screening operations where speed matters more than protection. These anti-BattleMech specialists are trained in the dangerous art of swarming enemy machines using grapling lines and powerful winches to target vulnerable joints and exposed systems that would normally be safely out of reach.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date based on prototype date for anti-Mek equipment
